The code statements that lead to the bug are:
css_put(wb->blkcg_css);
...
blkcg_unpin_online(wb->blkcg_css);
Reason:
The css_put() is called before blkcg_unpin_online(). If css_put() drops the last reference, the blkcg can be asynchronously freed (via css_free_rwork_fn -> blkcg_css_free -> kfree) before blkcg_unpin_online() dereferences the pointer to access blkcg->online_pin, resulting in a use-after-free.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
blkcg_unpin_online(wb->blkcg_css);
css_put(wb->blkcg_css);
Reason:
By moving blkcg_unpin_online() before css_put(), the blkcg structure is still alive (the CSS reference is still held) when it is accessed. css_put() is then called after the access, preventing the use-after-free.

